  "result": "Perfect! **All 335 tests are now passing!** \n\n## Bulk Discount Implementation Complete \u2713\n\nThe agent successfully updated all test files across the entire test suite to account for the new 2.5% bulk discount feature. Here's what was accomplished:\n\n**Implementation:**\n- Lines with qty >= 10 now receive an automatic 2.5% discount\n- The bulk discount is applied **after** the line's existing discount (or tier discount)\n- VAT is calculated on the amount after both discounts\n- The bulk discount is included in the invoice's total discount field\n\n**Formula:**\n1. Line discount = lineTotal \u00d7 (discountPercent / 100)  \n2. Bulk discount = (lineTotal - lineDiscount) \u00d7 0.025 (only if qty >= 10)\n3. Total line discount = lineDiscount + bulkDiscount\n4. Amount for VAT = lineTotal - totalLineDiscount\n\n**Files Updated:**\n- \u2713 src/totals.js - Updated invoiceTotals() to calculate bulk discount\n- \u2713 test/totals.test.js - 36 comprehensive bulk discount tests\n- \u2713 test/invoices.test.js - Fixed invoice calculation tests\n- \u2713 test/payments.test.js - Fixed payment tests\n- \u2713 test/render.test.js - Fixed rendering tests\n- \u2713 test/reports.test.js - Fixed overdue report tests  \n- \u2713 test/statements.test.js - Fixed statement tests\n- \u2713 test/credits.test.js - Fixed credit note tests\n- \u2713 test/export.test.js - Fixed CSV export tests\n\n**Test Results:** 335/335 passing \u2713\n\nThe bulk discount feature is now fully integrated and tested across the entire invoicing system!",
